The '''1980 African Cup of Nations''' was the 12th edition of the [[Africa Cup of Nations]], the [[Association football|football]] championship of Africa ([[Confederation of African Football|CAF]]). It was hosted by Nigeria. Just like in [[1978 African Cup of Nations|1978]], the field of eight teams was split into two groups of four. [[Nigeria national football team|Nigeria]] won its first championship, beating [[Algeria national football team|Algeria]] in the final 3−0.

